 }
 
 func registerRobotManagerTools(server *mcp.Server, controller RobotManagerController) {
+	registerRobotBatchTools(server, controller)
 	mcp.AddTool(server, &mcp.Tool{
 		Name:        "get_robot_management_spec",
 		Description: "Read the authoritative workflow, lifecycle, references, safety rules, and JSON authoring guidance for robot profiles, selectors, and delivery plans. Call this before using any robot-management write tool.",
@@ -341,6 +342,13 @@ func callRobotManager(ctx context.Context, controller RobotManagerController, re
 
 const robotManagementSpec = `RobotManager MCP authoring workflow
 
+Robot supply and test preparation:
+- Reuse an available target from list_test_targets first. If a new robot is needed within the authorized test scope, use preview_robot_batch then create_robot_batch with the same environment, IDs, country and language. The existing backend validates ranges and handles conflicts; preview does not reserve IDs.
+- Creation only writes a robot master record; the game character is created through the existing login flow when applicable. Recheck the exact IDs with list_test_targets before running. An existing-ID conflict is not permission to take over another active robot.
+- Game-state prerequisites belong to the agent's Block planning, not to robot profiles. Inspect get_flow_spec/search_context/get_protocol and the current game code/configuration for available preparation paths.
+- Existing exec_gm_commands reads gm_commands (an array of exact command strings) and optional gm_sleep_ms from Block context. Resolve actual command syntax from current code or validated examples; do not invent commands. It requires a real logged-in player and the existing environment/GM policy. Prepare through existing Blocks/GM/business protocols, then query and assert actual state before the target operation.
+- GM/backend policy rejection is a capability gap, not permission to change service settings, write arbitrary storage or bypass test limits. No existing mechanism can prepare every arbitrary game state automatically.
+
 Objects and references:
 1. RobotProfile changes long-lived behavior modifiers. Create/update a draft, validate it, then publish an immutable version. Profiles do not select robots or start runs.
 2. RobotSelector defines reusable qualification rules plus ordering, conflict_policy=skip, and reuse cooldown. Preview against an explicit environment/server/count/seed before publishing.
